{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments ["<b>As an eagle stirs up her nest.</b> He compared the Glory to an eagle, for it is king over all birds; so too the Glory is king over the separate intelligences, alluded to in the verse (Genesis 2:10): ״ומשם יפרד״ — 'and from there it parts.' And just as the eagle takes her young and bears them upon her pinion and leads them from place to place, so יהוה alone leads them — that is, Israel alone — and with Him there is no foreign El as partner from among all the separate supernal princes; as it is written (Psalms 73:25): ״מי לי בשמים, ועמך לא חפצתי בארץ״ — 'Who is for me in heaven? And with You I desire nothing on earth' — not angel or seraph, not star or constellation. And further: just as the eagle renews itself from time to time, in the manner of what is written (Isaiah 40:31): ״יעלו אבר כנשרים״, and (Psalms 103:5): ״תתחדש כנשר נעוריכי״, so too the Glory renews itself when the influx comes to it from above after it had been cut off from it through Israel's sin."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 32, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:53:07.625940267Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}